      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for openssh",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for openssh fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-73281: refused binding requests on locked SSH agents can allow destination restriction bypasses\n  (bsc#1275075).\n- CVE-2026-73282: unsynchronized remote forwarding updates in SSH client multiplexing can cause use-after-free\n  (bsc#1275074).\n- CVE-2026-73283: unenforced restriction keywords on tunnel forwarding can allow administrative security policy bypasses\n  (bsc#1275079).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
